---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout title="SproutLoud | Carlos Menco Guardo" mainClass="main-content main-content--project-detail" activePage="sproutloud" pageScripts={["/js/project-scroll-gradient.js"]}>
  <div class="content--sidebar">
    <div class="project-header">
      <div class="project-img-wrapper">
        <img src="/imgs/SproutLoud.svg" alt="SproutLoud website preview" />
      </div>
    </div>

    <section class="s1">
      <span class="project-detail-year">2018 - 2023</span>
      <h5 class="project-detail-title">SproutLoud Website</h5>
      <p class="project-detail-description">A corporate website rebuilt from scratch in WordPress, combining storytelling, structured content, marketing integrations, accessibility, SEO, and hiring workflows.</p>
      <a href="https://sproutloud.carlosmenco.site" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener" class="external-link">View demo <span class="external-link-icon"><svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 16 16" fill="none" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"><path d="M4.22876 4.22924V5.5586L9.49435 5.56332L3.75736 11.3003L4.70017 12.2431L10.4372 6.50613L10.4324 11.7717H11.7712V4.22924H4.22876Z" fill="currentColor"></path></svg></span></a>
    </section>

    <section class="s1">
      <h6>Overview</h6>
      <p>SproutLoud was a distributed marketing technology company later acquired by Ansira. The original site no longer exists publicly, so this portfolio keeps the work represented through a self-hosted semi-demo.</p>
      <p>I rebuilt the website from zero, redesigned the storytelling, and created a WordPress implementation that supported marketing pages, lead capture, accessibility requirements, SEO, and recruiting flows.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="s1">
      <h6>Role</h6>
      <p>WordPress development, ACF architecture, frontend implementation, storytelling redesign, Pardot form integration, SEO implementation, WCAG 2.0 accessibility work, and JazzHR API integration.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="s1">
      <h6>Challenge</h6>
      <p>The site needed to explain a complex B2B marketing platform in a clearer way while staying flexible for the marketing team. It also needed to connect with third-party systems for forms and careers without becoming fragile or difficult to maintain.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="s1">
      <h6>Solution</h6>
      <ul>
        <li>Redesigned the website narrative so product value, audiences, and business outcomes were easier to understand.</li>
        <li>Built reusable WordPress sections with ACF so marketing pages could be composed without custom code each time.</li>
        <li>Integrated Pardot forms for campaign and lead generation workflows.</li>
        <li>Implemented SEO and accessibility improvements aligned with WCAG 2.0 expectations.</li>
        <li>Connected JazzHR API data to support recruiting content and job listings.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section class="s1">
      <h6>Outcome</h6>
      <p>The final site gave SproutLoud a more flexible marketing platform and a clearer story for prospects, partners, and candidates. Even though the production site now redirects after the acquisition, the work remains one of my most complete WordPress builds.</p>
    </section>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
